# Citation metadata for the CFD loss-rate series (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# Zenodo's GitHub integration reads this file when a release is tagged.
# Data as of 2026-10-06 (7 figures updated 2026-10-13); release 2026-10-13 (provisional). Add the Zenodo DOI under
# `identifiers` once it is minted (concept DOI, so it always points to the latest version).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below. Credit TradingLookup and link to https://tradinglookup.com/brokers/cfd-loss-rates/"
type: dataset
title: "CFD loss-rate series"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-13"
authors:
  - name: "TradingLookup"
    website: "https://tradinglookup.com"
    email: "hello@tradinglookup.com"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://tradinglookup.com/brokers/cfd-loss-rates/"
abstract: >-
  The share of retail accounts that lose money, as each CFD provider states it in
  its own regulator-mandated risk warning. 31 providers whose sites were read from
  the UK on 2026-10-06 (7 figures updated on 2026-10-13 after a re-read in a UK
  browser), plus 404 archived quarterly figures for 18 providers from 2018-Q3
  (Wayback Machine). Data as of 2026-10-06; released 2026-10-13. Provisional: an
  independent automated second read on 2026-10-13 matched 16 of 31 figures; no
  figure has yet been re-read by a person. Each figure is the firm's own number;
  it is not adjusted, averaged or used to rank firms.
  Not investment advice.
keywords:
  - CFD
  - contracts for difference
  - retail investors
  - risk warning
  - loss rate
  - FCA
  - ESMA
  - open data
